1 NOTE Pedro de Noronha From 1419 through 1423 he was Bishop of Evora Portugal.
2 CONT From 1424 through 1452 was fourth Archbishop of Lisbon, Portugal.
2 CONT There are four acts of Legitimization of four of Pedro de Noronha's children,
2 CONT Joao, Diego also known as Rodrigo, Pedro and Isabel de Noronha, dated 1444. The children's mothers were named respectively, Isabel Diaz and Bianca Diaz, both single women. But, several historians have attributed these two women na
2 CONC med, Diaz to the surname of Perestrello. All of Pedro de Noronha's children held prominent positions in Portuguese aristocracy.
2 CONT Source on birthdate and death date as well as dates of service: Patriarchal See of Lisboa Portugal
2 CONT http://www.gcatholic.com/dioceses/diocese/lisbO.htm.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Braacamp Freire, Brazoes, Vol II p152, Faria, p 221, Freitas, pp 19-27, Peragalla, pp 11-17, Vignaud, pp 451-67,
2 CONT Documentos de Archivo Historico de Camara Municipal de Lisboa Vol II p 281, Vol 3 p 166.
2 CONT Bingo! Another connection made, semi legitimate via the Church. I don't recognize any church and this means I have to continue my research to establish a firmer and more legitimate ancestral connection.
2 CONT Research, 2005 John J. Browne Ayes, All Rights Reserved. national And International.
