1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogia_Gazzella
2 CONT
2 CONT Trogia Gazelle (also known as Trusia or Turzia; Gaeta, c. 1460 – Naples, 1511[2]) was an Italian noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a mistress of King Alfonso II of Naples and, through their children, mother-in-law of Lucrezia Borgia and Goffredo Borgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT She was the daughter of Antonio,[3] a nobleman from Gaeta and Orsina Carafa di Castelluccio. [4] She married Antonio Carbone in Naples and then, in 1495, Cesare Gesualdo di Capua. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT She went down in history for being the mistress of the King of Naples Alfonso II of Aragon, with whom she had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha of Aragon (born 1478 in Gaeta), who married Goffredo Borgia,[6] the illegitimate son of Pope Alexander VI and his mistress Vannozza Cattanei;
2 CONT Alfonso of Aragon (born in 1481 in Naples), Prince of Salerno, Duke of Bisceglie and second husband of Lucrezia Borgia. [7]
2 CONT The Aragonese dynasty, with its two sons, sanctioned the alliance with Pope Alexander VI Borgia, who intended to bring one of his sons to the throne of Naples. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/275230084/trogia-gazzella
