1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Alexander_VI
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pope Alexander VI''' (1 January 1431 – 18 August 1503) (Spanish: Alejandro VI, Catalan: Alexandre VI), born Roderic Llançol, later Roderic de Borja i Borja (Italian: Rodrigo Borgia) was Pope from 1492 to 1503. He is one of the 
2 CONC most controversial of the Renaissance popes, and his surname (Italianized as Borgia) became a byword for the debased standards of the papacy of that era.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Contents=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth and family 
2 CONT * Education and election 
2 CONT * Nepotism and opposition 
2 CONT * French involvement 
2 CONT * The French in retreat 
2 CONT * Confiscations and Savonarola 
