0 @N6000000002322298692@ NOTE This illegitimate son of Alfonso V succeeded to the throne of Naples upon his
1 CONT father's death, while Alfonso's brother, John II, king of Navarre from 1425,
1 CONT succeeded to the throne of Aragon. After his father became King of Naples in
1 CONT 1442, he had Ferdinand legitimized and recognized as his heir. Ferdinand had
1 CONT ongoing revolts with barons, finally suppressing them by a series of arrests,
1 CONT trials, confiscations, and executions.
